Body:
I've created #8658 which builds on this PR and addresses @rekram1-node's feedback from #8248.

**The key change:** Restricts `_noop` tool injection to only LiteLLM-backed providers instead of applying it unconditionally.

Detection logic:
```typescript
const isLiteLLMProxy =
  provider.options?.["litellmProxy"] === true ||
  input.model.providerID.toLowerCase().includes("litellm") ||
  input.model.api.id.toLowerCase().includes("litellm")
```

**Why this matters:**
- Your PR injects `_noop` for ALL providers unconditionally
- Per @rekram1-node's comment: "There are a LOT of providers that don't have this issue... ideally this would be strictly limited to litellm"
- My change adds auto-detection (provider ID contains "litellm") + explicit opt-in (`litellmProxy: true` option)

**Config example for custom gateways:**
```json
{
  "provider": {
    "my-gateway": {
      "options": { "litellmProxy": true }
    }
  }
}
```

Happy to discuss merging this into your PR or keeping them separate.

